+2.13. “Maximum Creeping Speed” means the maximum steady state speed which the vehicle achieves on a
+horizontal surface with the powertrain engaged and operating at idle, and no acceleration or brake demand.
+2.13.1. “Creeping” means the state of motion with the powertrain engaged and operating at idle, and no
+acceleration or brake demand, up to the Maximum Creeping Speed.
+2.14. "Reducing the effective demand of the accelerator control to zero" means where the resulting power/torque
+demand from the accelerator control is reduced to the equivalent of the driver removing any input into the
+accelerator control, irrespective of the actual input being given (this is exclusive of power/torque demand not in
+connection with the relative position of the accelerator control, e.g. rollback prevention, anti-stall).
 
